## Commands

Run everything from the repository root. No target asks for input; each ends with a reliable exit
code, and the multi-step ones print a summary of what passed and failed.

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `make doctor` | Checks uv{% if with_frontend %}, Node{% endif %}{% if with_database %} and Docker{% endif %}; says how to fix what is missing. |
| `make setup` | Installs dependencies{% if with_database %}, starts PostgreSQL, migrates{% endif %} and generates the API schema{% if with_frontend %} and types{% endif %}. Safe to repeat. |
| `make dev` | Runs the API on :8000{% if with_frontend %} and the visor on :5173{% endif %} with reload. |
| `make check` | Everything the CI checks. Must pass before a pull request. |
| `make test` | pytest{% if with_frontend %} and Vitest{% endif %}.{% if with_frontend %} `make e2e` runs Playwright.{% endif %} |
| `make fmt` | Formats and auto-fixes (ruff{% if with_frontend %}, oxfmt{% endif %}). |
| `make types` | Regenerates `backend/openapi.json`{% if with_frontend %} and `frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts`{% endif %}. Run it after any API change. |
{%- if with_database %}
| `make migrate` | Applies pending migrations to the local database. |
{%- endif %}

Single checks while working: `cd backend && uv run pytest tests/test_api.py -k healthz`{% if with_frontend %}, `cd frontend && npx playwright test e2e/home.spec.ts`{% endif %}.

## Before opening a pull request

1. `make fmt`, then `make check`. All steps must pass; the CI runs the same targets
   (`make check-backend`{% if with_frontend %}, `make check-frontend`{% endif %}).
2. If the API changed: `make types` and commit the regenerated files. The CI fails when they are stale.
3. Commit lockfiles (`backend/uv.lock`{% if with_frontend %}, `frontend/package-lock.json`{% endif %}) whenever dependencies change.

## Conventions

- **Small pull requests.** One task per branch and per pull request, against `main`. The
  description says what changes, why, what deserves attention in review and which checks passed.
  Commit messages are one sentence that describes the result.
- **Merge on green.** When the pull request is complete (final description, nothing left to
  decide), mark it with `gh pr merge --squash --auto`: GitHub merges it as soon as the required
  checks `Backend` and `Frontend` pass, and never if they fail. If the CI fails, fix and push; the
  mark stays.
- **Merging is deploying.** A push to `main` deploys{% if api_deploy == 'render' %} the API (Render waits for the CI){% elif api_deploy == 'railway' %} the API (Railway){% elif api_deploy == 'fastapi_cloud' %} the API (`deploy-api.yml`, after the CI){% elif api_deploy == 'vercel' %} {% if with_database %}through `deploy.yml` (migrate, then deploy){% else %}through Vercel's Git integration{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if with_frontend and api_deploy != 'vercel' %} and the visor (Vercel){% endif %}. Nothing is deployed by hand.
- **Check production after merging.** A task that touches `backend/` ends when production runs the
  new commit without errors: `cd backend && uv run {{ project_slug }} obs status --commit <merge commit> --wait 15`
  (exit 0: deployed, no errors; 1: errors since the deploy; 2: not deployed in time; 3: no read
  token, then say so and check by hand). Investigate any error before calling the task done. Do not
  poll production with `curl` meanwhile.
- **Tests.** Every new rule or route gets a pytest test; every visible behaviour of the visor a
  Playwright test{% if with_frontend %} (mocking `/api`){% endif %}; plain logic a unit test next to it.
{%- if with_database %}
- **Migrations.** A schema change is a new file `backend/src/{{ package_name }}/db/migrations/NNNN_short_name.sql`
  (next number). Never edit an applied migration: the runner stores checksums and refuses changed files.
  The runner is idempotent and takes a PostgreSQL advisory lock, so concurrent starts are safe.
{%- endif %}
- **Configuration.** New settings go in `settings.py` with a local default and the `{{ env_prefix }}` prefix,
  and in `backend/.env.example`. Secrets never enter the repository; everything runs locally without credentials.
- **No repeated work.** Read what the task needs, not every file. Run long commands (`make check`,
  Playwright) once at the end, in the background if your tool allows it, and do not spend turns
  saying they are still running.
- **Generated files.** `backend/openapi.json`{% if with_frontend %}, `frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts`{% endif %} and the lockfiles are generated:
  regenerate them, never edit them by hand.
- **Dependencies.** uv{% if with_frontend %} and npm{% endif %} only install releases that are at least 7 days old, and Dependabot
  waits as long: a compromised release is usually found and withdrawn within days. A newer version
  fails to resolve, so pick an older one. Exempting a package for an urgent fix needs the user's
  go-ahead: `exclude-newer-package = { <name> = false }` in `backend/pyproject.toml`{% if with_frontend %}, or
  `npm install --min-release-age=0 <name>@<version>` in `frontend/`{% endif %}.

## Deploy

{% if api_deploy == 'render' -%}
The API runs on Render (Docker, Frankfurt, free plan) from `render.yaml`.{% if with_database %} Migrations run when it
starts (`{{ env_prefix }}MIGRATE_ON_START`, on by default here): the free plan has no pre-deploy step.{% endif %}
{%- elif api_deploy == 'railway' -%}
The API runs on Railway (Docker, EU West) from `.railway/railway.ts`.{% if with_database %} Migrations run as Railway's
pre-deploy command (`{{ project_slug }} migrate`); a failure stops the deploy.{% endif %}
{%- elif api_deploy == 'fastapi_cloud' -%}
The API runs on FastAPI Cloud, deployed by `.github/workflows/deploy-api.yml` with `fastapi deploy`.
{%- if with_database %} Migrations run when the API starts (`{{ env_prefix }}MIGRATE_ON_START`, on by default here): FastAPI
Cloud has no pre-deploy command.{% endif %} The deployed commit reaches the app through `backend/DEPLOYED_COMMIT`, written by the workflow.
{%- elif api_deploy == 'vercel' -%}
Visor and API are one Vercel project and one domain (`vercel.json`); the API runs as Python functions.
{%- if with_database %} The database is Neon through its pooler (small pool per instance, no statement cache);
`deploy.yml` migrates with the direct connection string and then deploys.{% endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if with_database and api_deploy != 'vercel' %} Production PostgreSQL is Neon (EU region).{% endif %} Logfire receives the traces when `LOGFIRE_TOKEN` is set.
The one-time manual steps (accounts, secrets, variables) are in the README, "Deploy". Never create
or change cloud services without the user's explicit go-ahead.

## Template updates

The project can take later improvements of its template: with a clean worktree, run
`copier update --defaults` (add `--vcs-ref=HEAD` for the template's latest commit), resolve any
conflict markers, run `make setup` and `make check`, and open a pull request with the result.
